The present report describes the entire software engineering process followed and is organized around four main parts :
•  The First Part presents the project framework and context, introducing the host organization SOUTARAH GROUP, the existing system analysis, the objectives, the specifications and the task planning ;
• The Second Part is dedicated to the conceptual study, detailing the UP/UML methodological approach and the various design diagrams (use cases, activity, sequence and classes) ;
•  The Third Part develops the technical study, justifying the technological choices (React, React Native, Node.js, MySQL) and explaining the overall software architecture ;
•  The Fourth Part describes the practical implementation of the web platform and the mobile application, detailing the developed functionalities, validation tests, obtained results and the financial analysis of the project.

198:
Operationally, the project aims to :
•  Develop a modern web portal interactively presenting all 6 service units and the product catalog ;
•  Develop a native mobile application (Android / iOS) dedicated to real-time vehicle fleet consultation, fluid reservation with dynamic pricing and order status tracking ;
•  Implement a hybrid multi-item cart (vehicles and supplies) with an automated tax calculation engine (pre-tax, VAT 18%, TDT 2.5%) ;
•  Automate the generation of official pro-forma quotations in 2-page PDF format (with technical data sheets and visuals) ready for printing or electronic signature ;
•  Develop a centralized administration dashboard (Back-Office) for managing quotations, vehicles, customers and notifications ;
•  Integrate a transactional email notification system.

201:
The specifications formalize the functional and non-functional requirements of the interconnected system :
1. Functional requirements for the Client (Web & Mobile) :
  •  Detailed consultation of the vehicle and product catalog by category ;
  •  Multi-criteria filtering of vehicles (brand, type, transmission, air conditioning) ;
  •  Selection of rental dates with dynamic calculation according to the destination pricing (Abidjan / Outside Abidjan) and the driver option ;
  •  Shopping cart / reservation management and one-click validation ;
  •  Instant download of the official PDF pro-forma quotation complying with the company's legal charter ;
  •  Personal quotation management area ;

202:
2. Functional requirements for the Administrator :
  •  Global supervision of key indicators (estimated turnover, active reservations) ;
  •  Complete vehicle fleet management (addition, modification, maintenance status) ;
  •  Complete trading product management (adding products, modifying prices) ;
  •  Customer account management and partner discount allocation.
3. Technical requirements and constraints :
  •  Security ;
  •  Availability and performance ;
  •  Portability : Compatibility with modern browsers (Chrome, Safari, Edge) and mobile devices.

